    "body": "Coordinator: the cause is known. The post does not lose a needed tool change. The shipped example is stale. My merge of PR #3464 made `main` red.\n\n## Facts\n- `examples/first-router-part.nc` on `main` has three sections: `Drill1` with T1 (`T1 M6`, line 7), `2D Pocket1` with T2 (`T2 M6`, line 23) and `2D Contour1` with T2 again (`T2 M6`, line 82).\n- The line that is absent from the posted output is line 82: the second `T2 M6`, for a section that keeps the tool of the section before it.\n- PR #3464 (merged as 995337a66, issue #3445) makes the grbl-family posts keep a repeated tool: a section with the same tool gets no second tool call and no stop for a manual change. The lift, the tool comment and the new `S M3` stay. This is the behaviour that #3445 asked for, and a review and a second read checked it.\n- So the first tool change to T2 (line 23) is still posted. The program is correct. One line of the shipped file is stale.\n\n## Why the trial did not see it\nThe trial merge of #3464 ran the whole quick plan (60 steps), the whole post crate, `golden_cl`, `posting`, the router binaries (`first_router_part` is one of them and it passed) and the three example catalog suites. The test binary `first_part_programs`, which compares the shipped files under `examples/`, is not in the quick plan for a post script change and was not in my list. This is the gate gap of #3521, for a second set of files.\n\n## What to do (for the session that claimed this issue)\n1. Make `examples/first-router-part.nc` again with the tool of the example (one commit; the diff must be the one line 82 and nothing more). Check the other shipped example programs of the grbl-family posts (`grbl`, `grblhal`, `tinyg`) for a second section with the same tool: `first_part_programs` shows them.\n2. The priority: this is a red `main` with a correct program, so `P2` by the table, not `P1`. I do not change the label of a claimed issue; the claimant can.\n3. No change of the post.\n\nI add `first_part_programs` to the list of #3521.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
